# Every checkout gets the bytes that were committed. Spec vectors, annexes and fixtures are
# checked by SHA-256, so a Windows checkout converting LF to CRLF would fail them.
* text=auto eol=lf
crates/qso-graph-interop-ffi/include/qso_graph_interop.h text eol=lf
# Live captures are stored exactly as recorded (a Windows recorder wrote CRLF lines); their SHA-256 pins
# are of those bytes, so no end-of-line conversion either way.
crates/qso-graph-interop/tests/fixtures/live-captures/*.ndjson -text
